# Jira + doc API test agent

This repo is the Salesforce API QA platform. When asked to generate or run API tests from a Jira story and an integration document, **drive this app** — do not author a separate Postman collection as the source of truth.

## Topology

1. **In-app engine** (`server/engine/generator.js` `generateSuite`, `runner.js`, `assertions.js`) is executable truth.
2. **In-app Cursor CLI then Gemini CLI** (`cli-generator.js`) may add scenarios from the story + `context_docs`. Prefer Cursor if logged in.
3. **Cursor IDE Agent** orchestrates config, docs, and HTTP calls to this server. Do not use a Gemini Cursor subagent as the runtime generator. This app rejects Gemini/Cursor API keys; login is CLI session only.
4. **Human approval** of `/api/proposals/:id/approve` is required for story suites. Never auto-approve. Never auto-create Jira defects.

## Inputs

- Jira key (`PROJ-123`) via existing sync/`getIssue` — not invented tickets.
- Integration doc via `POST /api/projects/:id/context-docs` (paste or local path). No remote URL fetch, Confluence, or Jira attachments in v1.
- Optional OpenAPI via contracts / `endpoints/from-openapi`.

## Output JSON (CLI / any generator)

Must match `normalizeTestCase` in `server/engine/cli-generator.js`:

```json
{
  "scenarios": [{
    "title": "string",
    "type": "Functional|Negative|Boundary|Security|Integration|Contract",
    "apiType": "REST",
    "object": "Account",
    "label": "ASSUMED",
    "testCases": [{
      "title": "string",
      "method": "GET|POST|PUT|PATCH|DELETE|HEAD",
      "endpoint": "/services/data/vXX.X/sobjects/Account",
      "auth": "default",
      "assertions": [{ "type": "status", "op": "eq", "expected": 201 }],
      "body": {},
      "query": {}
    }]
  }]
}
```

Do not invent Salesforce objects/fields absent from describe. No secrets. Labels: **VERIFIED** (live describe/org only), **ASSUMED** (heuristics/demo/CLI), **RECOMMENDED** (AI extras).

## Guardrails

- Production writes need `confirmProductionWrites`; DELETE needs a second confirm (`safety.js`).
- Do not edit Postman-gap files (http-lab, auth-apply, cookie-jar, script-sandbox, environments, curl, grpc, ws-sessions, mock-server) unless the user asked for those features.
- Pass/fail comes from the runner after approve, not from the model.

If the user wants unattended generation, use sync-and-generate then stop for human review — do not set approve=true (that flag is a no-op and must stay a no-op until an explicit product change).
